You can type this in the dictionary too.

00:04:43.551 --> 00:04:49.535
As a side note, to enter the sun symbol you need to copy and paste it, unless your keyboard has a sun on it.

00:04:49.535 --> 00:04:55.175
With that little change, we're now up to 26% compression.

00:04:55.175 --> 00:04:59.519
Try it yourself and see if you can do better.

00:04:59.519 --> 00:05:04.559
song lyric or poem is obvious, but really any form of information can have repetition

00:05:04.559 --> 00:05:07.979
or patterns in it. They're just not as obvious.

00:05:07.979 --> 00:05:09.439
For example, an outdoor

00:05:09.503 --> 00:05:14.063
The door's phono can have a blue sky, and instead of storing every single blue pixel,

00:05:14.063 --> 00:05:15.803
that can be compressed.

00:05:15.803 --> 00:05:19.487
With the amount of information that's digitized and sent around the internet every day,

00:05:19.487 --> 00:05:24.127
there are much fancier ways to compress the data. Data compression is now built

00:05:24.127 --> 00:05:28.247
into how every picture, a song, or movie is stored, and almost every webpage you

00:05:28.247 --> 00:05:29.447
visit is compressed as it's

00:05:29.471 --> 00:05:31.791
sent to your device.

00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:34.671
All these compression algorithms have one thing in common.

00:05:34.671 --> 00:05:39.231
They all aim to represent the information in the smallest format possible, in a way

00:05:39.231 --> 00:05:39.455
that

00:05:39.455 --> 00:05:44.335
can be decompressed to reconstruct the original, or at least something close to it.

